PART D: EVENT SERVICE (src/services/event.service.js)
1. toPublicEvent(eventDoc): a whitelist for public and customer responses: id, title, description, venueName, city, startsAt, registrationOpensAt, registrationClosesAt, totalTickets, pricePaise, maxPerUser, holdMinutes, status, phase (see 6), soldOut (boolean computed from the counters), maxResalePricePaise (computed with calculateMaxResalePrice from utils/money.js), publishedAt, organizerName (the organizer's name only). NEVER include organizerId, organizer email or phone, held-ticket counts or any internal counter. toOwnerEvent(eventDoc) adds organizerId-free management fields (ticketsAvailable, ticketsSold, ticketsHeld, cancelReason, cancelledAt) and is used only for the owner and ADMIN.
2. createEvent(organizerId, input, requestMeta): creates a DRAFT with counters initialised and organizerId from the authenticated user (never from the body). SecurityLog EVENT_CREATED.
3. updateEvent(eventId, actor, input, requestMeta):
   - Load the event. If it does not exist, or the actor is an ORGANIZER who is not the owner, return HTTP 404 NOT_FOUND. For the not-owner case write SecurityLog EVENT_ACCESS_DENIED (with eventId and actor id) before returning the same 404.
   - ORGANIZER may edit only their own events. ADMIN may NOT edit event content (admins can only cancel). An ADMIN edit attempt returns 403 FORBIDDEN.
   - While status is DRAFT, every allowed field may change (re-run the same time-order validation on the merged values).
   - After DRAFT (published or later), ONLY description may change. Any other field in the body returns 409 EVENT_LOCKED with a message "After publishing, only the description can be changed. Cancel and recreate the event to change other details." Do not partially apply anything.
   - Cancelled events cannot be edited (409 EVENT_LOCKED).
   - Apply the update ATOMICALLY with findOneAndUpdate where the filter includes _id, organizerId and the status you read (so a concurrent publish cannot sneak in between). If it matches nothing, re-read and return the correct 404 or 409.
   - SecurityLog EVENT_UPDATED listing the changed field NAMES only.
4. publishEvent(eventId, actor, requestMeta): only the owning ORGANIZER. ATOMIC transition with findOneAndUpdate filter { _id, organizerId, status: DRAFT, registrationClosesAt: { $gt: now } }, setting status PUBLISHED and publishedAt. If nothing matched: not found or not owner -> 404; status not DRAFT -> 409 INVALID_EVENT_STATE; registration already closed -> 409 EVENT_REGISTRATION_ALREADY_CLOSED. Two simultaneous publish requests must produce exactly one success. SecurityLog EVENT_PUBLISHED.
5. cancelEvent(eventId, actor, { reason }, requestMeta): owning ORGANIZER or ADMIN. Reason: plain string 3 to 300 characters (required). Allowed only from the statuses that EVENT_STATUS_TRANSITIONS lists as cancellable. Guard: if any Booking or Ticket document exists for this event, return 409 EVENT_HAS_BOOKINGS ("Events with bookings cannot be cancelled yet. Refund handling is not built in this version."). ATOMIC transition with the status condition in the filter. SecurityLog EVENT_CANCELLED (the reason text is allowed in the log details; it contains no personal data). A comment must say that the guard exists because refunds and contract-side cancellation are not designed yet.
6. getEventPhase(event, now = new Date()): a PURE function returning one of: "DRAFT", "UPCOMING" (published, registration not open yet), "REGISTRATION_OPEN", "REGISTRATION_CLOSED", "CANCELLED". Based on status and the registration timestamps only. Add a comment that Prompts 11 and 12 will add queue and booking phases, and that status stays the stored source of truth while phase is a derived display value. If ARCHITECTURE.md already defines these phases or statuses, align names with it and report.
7. listPublicEvents({ page, limit, city, q }): returns { items, page, limit, total, totalPages }.
   - Only events whose status is not DRAFT and not CANCELLED. Sort by startsAt ascending, then _id for a stable order.
   - page: integer >= 1 (default 1). limit: integer 1 to EVENT_LIST_MAX_PAGE_SIZE (default EVENT_LIST_DEFAULT_PAGE_SIZE). Invalid values return 400 VALIDATION_ERROR (do not silently clamp strings to something odd; objects/arrays from query strings such as city[$ne]=x must be rejected with 400, because Express can parse them into objects).
   - city: plain string up to 60 characters, case-insensitive exact match. q: plain string up to 50 characters, case-insensitive "contains" match on title, built from an ESCAPED string (escape every regex special character) so that q=".*" or "(a+)+$" matches only those literal characters. Use lean queries and select only the whitelisted fields.
8. getPublicEvent(eventId, viewer): DRAFT events are visible only to the owner and ADMIN (404 for everyone else including logged-out users and other organizers). CANCELLED events are visible to everyone (so people with an old link see why it is gone). Public responses use toPublicEvent.
9. listMyEvents(organizerId, { page, limit, status }): all of the organizer's own events (including DRAFT and CANCELLED), newest first, using toOwnerEvent, with the same pagination rules. status filter must be a value from the enum.

